## Input and Output in C++

### Key Components

* `cin` → Input stream.
* `cout` → Output stream.
* `endl` or `\n` → New line.

### Example

```cpp
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    int age;
    float height;
    char grade;
    string name;

    cin >> age >> height >> grade >> name;

    cout << "Your age: " << age << "\n";
    cout << "Your height: " << height << "\n";
    cout << "Your grade: " << grade << "\n";
    cout << "Your name: " << name << "\n";

    return 0;
}
```

### Input

```text
20 5.9 A Alice
```

### Output

```text
Your age: 20
Your height: 5.9
Your grade: A
Your name: Alice
```

